's all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on September 5, 2000.","t_chg":"Galveston has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 146 complete years: Galveston's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.15), about +1.7\u00b0F since 1875. Galveston's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.20\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.25), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1875.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Galveston's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.19 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 46.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1900 (78.39 in); the driest, 1948 (21.40 in). Galveston almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}